2026-07-07 13:40:18,256 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: The proposed AI solution for this municipal agent assistance project would leverage our company's expertise in large language models, specifically our preferred sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong performance in French-language tasks and complies with EU regulations. 

We would fine-tune the Mistral 7B model using our established methods such as LoRA or QLoRA to adapt it to the specific tone, format, and domain knowledge required for municipal administrative tasks. This approach is expected to yield an average accuracy gain of 12% compared to a non-fine-tuned model.

To enhance information retrieval and consultation capabilities, we would integrate Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) techniques, utilizing our experience with vector stores like Qdrant or Weaviate. This would enable the model to provide more accurate and relevant information to municipal agents by retrieving from a knowledge base of administrative documents and regulations.

For drafting administrative contents and instructing files, the fine-tuned Mistral 7B model would generate high-quality text based on the input prompts and context provided by the agents. Collaboration and continuity of processing would be facilitated through a user interface that allows agents to interact with the AI system seamlessly, providing feedback and corrections that could further improve the model's performance over time.

Explainability and trust are crucial in this application, so we would implement source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring. Actions for low-confidence outputs would include displaying uncertainty warnings and escalating to human supervisors, ensuring transparency and reliability in the decision-making process.

This solution aligns with our past successes in delivering AI-powered assistants for regulatory document Q&A, contract review, clinical guideline assistance, and data synthesis for urban planners, demonstrating our capability to adapt AI technologies to various domains and use cases. By addressing known trade-offs such as explicability vs. performance and model size vs. energy consumption, we can provide a balanced solution that meets both the functional requirements of municipal agents and the compliance standards of the EU AI Act.
